Z||000004||Carrolles||02-28-2000||11:14 PM||||Does your A/C work now?  There is a small two wire rectangular connector that plugs into the A/C clutch.<P>How many wires is in the connector and can you see the colors of the wires?  Do you have auto or standard trans?||||reg||1
Z||000005||chris6878||02-28-2000||11:18 PM||||Yep.. that sounds like it...   2 wire, rectangular, hangs right beside the a/c pump... but where would it connect at?   Not much room there to look around to see...  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||3
Z||000006||b_b_a_d||02-29-2000||01:04 AM||||If memory serves me right...  It is on the back side of the a/c clutch toward the center rear.  I did it with the cradle out and sitting on a pallet.  It shouldn't be to hard to find from the bottom if you jack up the car and convienantly have a creeper handy.  Not a very good pic, but something to give you an idea just where the a/c cluth is in relation to the cradle.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86_cradle.jpg" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/86_cradle.jpg</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by b_b_a_d (edited 02-29-2000).]||||reg||3
